# Maintenance task schedule — 5-field Vixie cron: min hour dom mon dow
# Trigger any job immediately with: POST /jobs/<name>
# Times are local server time. Override this file with --schedule <path>.

0 0 * * 0   backup          # weekly, Sunday 00:00
0 2 * * 1   rba-fx-import   # weekly, Monday 02:00
0 3 1 * *   mic-import      # monthly, 1st at 03:00 (ISO publishes monthly)
0 4 1 * *   currency-import # monthly, 1st at 04:00 (ISO 4217 + ISO 24165 / DTIF)

# Closing prices, twice daily: each run stores the latest complete trading day
# per held listing and skips days already stored ok, so the two runs cover the
# different market closes between them (assuming a Sydney server clock):
# 17:30 catches the 16:00 ASX close; 11:30 catches the prior NYSE close
# (06:00-08:00 Sydney) and the crypto UTC-midnight cut-off (10:00-11:00 Sydney).
30 17 * * 1-5  price-import # weekdays, after the ASX close
30 11 * * *    price-import # daily, after the NYSE close + crypto UTC cut-off

# Report snapshots, daily after the 11:30 price import: stores the
# price-dependent reports for the latest date every held listing can be
# valued at with final prices (typically yesterday once the prior NYSE close
# and crypto UTC cut-off are in). Skips a date already stored fresh;
# regenerates it when flagged stale.
0 12 * * *     report-snapshot
